{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk","id":1555313,"title":"What if a Lupus Garou bred with a human kinfolk?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-10T08:10:11-08:00","id":1555313,"title":"What if a Lupus Garou bred with a human kinfolk?","content":"It would be an interesting premise having a character who finds out their dad was a Wolf that fell in love with a human woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-10-2025, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T08:45:27-08:00","id":1555314,"title":"","content":"Nothing<br /> Really.. nothing strange<br /> Lupus born Garou are like all the other Garou<br /> They can fell in love, emotionally they are the same as any other, the First change boost that Wolf brain a bit up to the Human level in terms of sentience and Consciousness<br /> They can learn, they can talk, they can love, they are like any other Garou... just they born as a Wolf<br /> Love usually not a factor in a Kinfolk (or human... or some cases, a Spirit) and Garou relationship but not unheard of either<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T10:08:33-08:00","id":1555319,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking about the weird family dynamic of a guy after his first change finding out that his dad was born a Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T10:21:15-08:00","id":1555321,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re quite right - and I suspect it\u2019s a peculiar situation that\u2019s played out in many, many variations over the history of the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s especially interesting to wonder if some Lupus Garou tend to favour Human lovers, as a way to \u2018sow their wild oats\u2019 without disrupting the dynamic of a wolf pack, applying a far lesser degree of interest towards children of such unions - or if they take a human lover because they\u2019re interested in a somewhat committed relationship, but cannot spare the time to serve as Father to a wolf pack.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d bet this is more of a tendency in male Lupus than in females - given wolf pregnancy is a lesser commitment of time than what a human mother endures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T14:04:47-08:00","id":1555329,"title":"","content":"So, ultimately, I think this is going to be less interesting than it sounds in the default nature of the setting (being as edition agnostic as possible). The big reason why this isn't going to be that interesting is because it will pretty much always get overshadowed by something else.<br /> <br /> First, lets start with a the children of Garou raised in Garou society (because Garou or Kinfolk doesn't really change much here). Having a wolf ancestor in modern times is considered a good thing by most of the Tribes, and a neutral things by the few that don't value it. Even if no Tribe takes it as far as the Red Talons, they all fundamentally agree that modern Garou are losing touch with their wolf-side. The majority view is that trying to rebalance that in homid bloodlines is obviously good (though the Red Talons would argue too little too late), with the minority view simply not caring (the Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, and Stargazers being the Tribes most associated with this side). So, a kid raised in Garou social norms is going to think having a recent wolf ancestor is a good thing - or at least that most other people in their social circles think it's a good thing - and knowing your family lineage is an important social custom; again even if you don't particularly value it the larger society does. So a young Child of Gaia learning about Garou culture and their family lineage is going to find out really fast if they have a wolf-parent, and are going to be acclimated to the idea that this is a positive thing.<br /> <br /> What's going to matter is how this impacts the relationship between parent and child. But... &quot;lupus vs homid&quot; is quickly going to take a backseat to so many other issues facing all Garou-child relationships: how present is the Garou when there's a war to fight? Does that Garou do well as a parent despite things like having Rage, are they a tyrant expecting strict familial obedience, or where-ever between those? But every Garou parent can fall into these categories. Lupus fathers have strong parental instincts and the ability to learn how to parent as a human, while plenty of homid fathers use the war against the Wyrm as an excuse to be deadbeats and pawn child rearing on the Kinfolk. The fact that Ranked Garou and their children (Cubs or Kin) basically live in fundamentally different worlds means that disconnect is always going to overshadow something like, &quot;wait, dad's a wolf?&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, we can look to the opposite side of things with a Lost Cub; easily the result of something like Atticus suggested of a Lupus father opting to have a lot of kids with a lot of human mothers. But lets face it, if you're growing up thinking you're a perfectly normal kid with a deadbeat dad that's never been in the picture... and then things change when you find out you're actually a werewolf... is the fact that your dad was born a wolf really going to register as a shock compared to everything else you have to deal with when you're suddenly thrust into Garou society?<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's going to get overshadowed. There is so much going on for a Lost Cub getting adjusted to Garou life that having a wolf for a dad is just... not going to have space to matter.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that it's a bad dynamic to explore if you want, but I do think it's a bit too easy to fall into the trap of how shocking it would be for us, the real people playing the game, vs. how shocking it would be for the actual characters in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T15:58:53-08:00","id":1555338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555319#post1555319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about the weird family dynamic of a guy after his first change finding out that his dad was born a Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>His dad is a werewolf will matter a lot more.<br /> <br /> In addition to what others already said, I'd just add that the setting already assumes that happens with some regularity (if not as much as before).<br /> <br /> Garou society expects as default that everyone have as many children as possible and with both humans and wolves. Obviously it doesn't happen nearly as much as it should, but it does happen regularly, and Lupus Garou in particular don't seem to have as much of a problem doing it as Homid do.<br /> <br /> So... yeah. Homid Garou with a wolf-born parent is a thing that happens frequently enough already.<br /> <br /> And Garou aren't humans or wolves, they're Garou from birth, for whatever that matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T16:30:31-08:00","id":1555340,"title":"","content":"A good bit of semantic pedantry for these sorts of conversations of &quot;normal&quot; vs &quot;normative.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something &quot;normal&quot; is something common that a decent majority within a group are going to experience. Something &quot;normative&quot; can be extremely rare to actually have happen, but is something ingrained as part of the structure of a culture. The coronation of a new monarch on the death of the last monarch can be very abnormal, but still be completely normative. A monarch could sit on a throne long enough for a whole generation to have never known another ruler, but the succession is baked into a monarch so once the monarch finally dies, the process is already in place so nobody gets shocked or confused by what happens next.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of things in Garou society that are normative, but not necessarily &quot;normal.&quot; Though this can be a bit obscured by the exceptional nature of the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T18:55:25-08:00","id":1555344,"title":"","content":"Well, what I mean is that he knew his dad, he thought his dad was an ordinary guy because he became accustomed to human society to be a good father and husband. So imagine thinking your entire life that your dad was as normal as can be until you find out he was essentially a wolf living as a man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T22:11:36-08:00","id":1555349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555344#post1555344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what I mean is that he knew his dad, he thought his dad was an ordinary guy because he became accustomed to human society to be a good father and husband. So imagine thinking your entire life that your dad was as normal as can be until you find out he was essentially a wolf living as a man.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's the problem. His dad being a werewolf matters much more on a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> His dad is a werewolf is a big enough reveal to begin with, being wolf-born is just extra spice if that much.<br /> <br /> Not only that, the child is a werewolf too, and has far more to deal with than how their dad was born.<br /> <br /> Being dragged to a Caern and learning what all that means, finding out what their dad may have left undone to dedicate so much to child rearing, there's just too much going on.<br /> <br /> This revelation may get you an awkward scene at best, but will be overshadowed too soon by everything else happening.<br /> <br /> You can get some more mileage out of this with a kinfolk child instead of a Garou. They'll still live in human society as humans. Maybe a plot that reveals the father was born a wolf before revealing he's a werewolf can milk this strangeness longer. But again, once it's revealed that their dad is a werewolf, that kind of explains and overshadows &quot;dad was a wolf&quot; as far as strangeness and shock goes. At most it may look that those things are related, dad is a werewolf <i>because</i> he's a wolf, but unless werewolf stuff stays mostly out of the way, the wolf-born part won't be relevant for long.<br /> <br /> Still something that happens with some regularity in the setting. Not a lot, but happens. It would take a fairly weird Lupus Garou to raise a child personally and still not teach them about Garou society at all, but Lupus are still people and people do weird shit.<br /> <br /> For whatever that matters, by the way, this can play out with the mom just as easily. The child of a Garou takes on the form of the non-Garou parent anyway, so mom will have a normal human pregnancy even if she was born a wolf, and has a slightly higher chance of staying around after the birth of the child, specially if the human father is a deadbeat dad anyway to begin with and she has to resort to her own family as support. Theoretically you could have a single mother that's a wolf easier than a father that's a wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T23:44:14-08:00","id":1555352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555349#post1555349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For whatever that matters, by the way, this can play out with the mom just as easily. The child of a Garou takes on the form of the non-Garou parent anyway, so mom will have a normal human pregnancy even if she was born a wolf</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was only a weird thing that happened with Rokea. Some kind of difficult re-merging with humanity or the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and has a slightly higher chance of staying around after the birth of the child, specially if the human father is a deadbeat dad anyway to begin with and she has to resort to her own family as support. </div> </div> </div>I AM THE STORM THAT IS ESCAPING<br /> EVADING PARENTAL OBLIGATIONS<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Theoretically you could have a single mother that's a wolf easier than a father that's a wolf. </div> </div> </div>Going to be less than pleasant either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-11-2025, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T00:07:29-08:00","id":1555353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555352#post1555352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to be less than pleasant either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming a parent with Rage no higher than 3, Willpower 8+ and very supportive family and/or friends to begin with, because the whole scenario is quite unlikely to end well when, you know, your actually present and ok parent is a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also no dots in Primal Urge and whatever it takes to lessen the Curse as much as possible.<br /> <br /> We'd need a very well thought build for this Garou, a &quot;good parent combo&quot; isn't easy to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T14:42:59-08:00","id":1555690,"title":"","content":"I had a character idea that played off of that, combined with him being the unwitting (and idiotic) son of a Black Spiral Dancer Ragabash: He'd be joining the party in Story 1/Session 1, fresh from his First change, with the idea that the party was passing by, and found him while on their way to a completely unrelated destination. He wouldn't even have gone through his Rite of Passage yet to boot (with the idea that the tribe he'd fall into, would feel natural as I settled into the character and role-played him). Plus, I did NOT give him his starting Auspice and Tribal gifts to reflect this decision - He'd only have his Homid gift.<br /> <br /> Combined with his Idiot Flaw and Common Sense Merit, I had a whole sales pitch ready for whatever Storyteller on how to drop subtle hints and stuff (with the father being an active background character who'd subtlety screw with the group as well as manipulate events, spirits, and people who interact with the party), so veteran players with attention to detail would have fun picking apart details relating to this character, while I'd roleplay a 21 year old average Joe, Mr Magoo-ing his way around being a Werewolf - let alone being a Garou.<br /> <br /> Another detail I'm proud that I had prepped was that he was afraid of mirrors, because his dad would (in Crinos form) sneak into his room via a giant mirror on regular occasion, for literally no purpose but to just scare the shit out of him and being a massive troll.<br /> <br /> I had everything worked out, but then I couldn't find a group of players to play Werewolf with, so all that effort just kinda died in the water.<br /> <br /> I actually forgot about it all until this post, oddly enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T20:40:48-08:00","id":1555703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaFrontlineSpecter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555690#post1555690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, I did NOT give him his starting Auspice and Tribal gifts to reflect this decision - He'd only have his Homid gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>A character fresh out of the First Change wouldn't actually have any Gift whatsoever. Even the first three Gifts still come from the spirits during a Garou first forays into the Umbra and the establishment of their initial place in Garou society. You would be better off having no Gift to begin with, but wouldn't have to pay for the first three you're entitled as a starting character.<br /> <br /> I'd be wary of an exceedingly dumb character with a too-present NPC because this has some potential to hijack the chronicle, but can't say for sure without more info. It does look like a fun character, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T21:53:43-08:00","id":1555707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555703#post1555703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A character fresh out of the First Change wouldn't actually have any Gift whatsoever. Even the first three Gifts still come from the spirits during a Garou first forays into the Umbra and the establishment of their initial place in Garou society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wish pre-Rite of Passage / First Change stories were more common and shared, because no matter how many books I read, big details like that keep slipping under my nose. lol<br /> <br /> But I do appreciate you bringing that to my attention! I'll keep that in mind. Thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555703#post1555703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be wary of an exceedingly dumb character with a too-present NPC because this has some potential to hijack the chronicle, but can't say for sure without more info. It does look like a fun character, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you mentioned that, because I foresaw that and designed the father NPC <b>very specifically</b> to avoid that exact issue. Any NPC part of a player characters' backstory should compliment what the ST already had/has planned, not hijack it (Gift: Blur of the Milky Eye makes this a wee bit easier for the storyteller).<br /> <br /> Plus, if the pacing of the current story ever grinds to a standstill, the father can get up to &quot;just a little bit of trolling&quot; to get the pacing of the Chronicle back up to cadence (or at least that's the idea), and overall was designed to <b>prevent </b>Chronicle-hijacking in mind, in advance. <hr /><br /> <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Back to </span>Samuelalpha86</a>'s original question:</b><br /> <br /> I didn't mean to hijack the conversation, but for my two cents on adding to the original conversation that this thread is about<b></b>: If anyone wants to make a Homid Garou (or a Homid Kinfolk) character with a Lupus-born Garou parent, it's already just &quot;normal-ish&quot; in Garou society (even though it's not a common occurrence for obvious reasons) as stated earlier in the thread, so, you're gonna need to add something else to make that detail worth anything more and give it sustenance other than &quot;cool detail, bro&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why not have the character's Lupus parent also be their Mentor (a la Background of same name)? Could flushing out this other character add anything to the Story that your players will be playing in (and by extension - the Chronicle)?<br /> <br /> Because as a player option, yes, you can, but if you're not going to go the full 9 yards with it and have it actually add anything to the character, then why are you bothering?<br /> <br /> Did this Lupus parent visit their child in the cradle in Hispo form and grant your player character a phobia flaw relating to big dogs? STUFF LIKE THAT!<br /> <br /> My best advice is <i><b>&quot;make it mean something, so it sticks around in the long term&quot;</b></i>.<br /> Maybe it can be a downtime exercise - maybe this homid character has a ton of Lupus-breed half-siblings that he now needs to figure out what to do with, and the player pack can be involved in some way where shenanigans ensue.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if my advice makes sense, but I hope it helps the original poster, and I hope it helps anybody who reads this thread due to having the same question!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T01:40:04-08:00","id":1555788,"title":"","content":"To answer the OP's post in my own headworld rework of the breeds It would basically result in a canon crinos-born (with the corresponding Lantry tenant on garou pairing being changed to Don't do bestiality). Normal (ex: Humanoid x Humanoid and Lupus X Lupus) pairings would result in a &quot;normal&quot; child born in crinos form, Granted garous tend to have extermly low rates of conception with breed x breed parings compared to kin x kin pairings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T06:58:41-08:00","id":1555795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaFrontlineSpecter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555707#post1555707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really wish pre-Rite of Passage / First Change stories were more common and shared, because no matter how many books I read, big details like that keep slipping under my nose. lol<br /> <br /> But I do appreciate you bringing that to my attention! I'll keep that in mind. Thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Funny you mentioned that, because I foresaw that and designed the father NPC <b>very specifically</b> to avoid that exact issue. Any NPC part of a player characters' backstory should compliment what the ST already had/has planned, not hijack it (Gift: Blur of the Milky Eye makes this a wee bit easier for the storyteller).<br /> <br /> Plus, if the pacing of the current story ever grinds to a standstill, the father can get up to &quot;just a little bit of trolling&quot; to get the pacing of the Chronicle back up to cadence (or at least that's the idea), and overall was designed to <b>prevent </b>Chronicle-hijacking in mind, in advance. <hr /><br /> <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Back to </span>Samuelalpha86</a>'s original question:</b><br /> <br /> I didn't mean to hijack the conversation, but for my two cents on adding to the original conversation that this thread is about<b></b>: If anyone wants to make a Homid Garou (or a Homid Kinfolk) character with a Lupus-born Garou parent, it's already just &quot;normal-ish&quot; in Garou society (even though it's not a common occurrence for obvious reasons) as stated earlier in the thread, so, you're gonna need to add something else to make that detail worth anything more and give it sustenance other than &quot;cool detail, bro&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why not have the character's Lupus parent also be their Mentor (a la Background of same name)? Could flushing out this other character add anything to the Story that your players will be playing in (and by extension - the Chronicle)?<br /> <br /> Because as a player option, yes, you can, but if you're not going to go the full 9 yards with it and have it actually add anything to the character, then why are you bothering?<br /> <br /> Did this Lupus parent visit their child in the cradle in Hispo form and grant your player character a phobia flaw relating to big dogs? STUFF LIKE THAT!<br /> <br /> My best advice is <i><b>&quot;make it mean something, so it sticks around in the long term&quot;</b></i>.<br /> Maybe it can be a downtime exercise - maybe this homid character has a ton of Lupus-breed half-siblings that he now needs to figure out what to do with, and the player pack can be involved in some way where shenanigans ensue.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if my advice makes sense, but I hope it helps the original poster, and I hope it helps anybody who reads this thread due to having the same question!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I thought that maybe this scenario would involve the Garou being of the Japanese Hakken Tribe who are heavily influenced by human culture and have their own secret hidden packs of Japanese Wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T17:22:28-08:00","id":1556208,"title":"","content":"I just realized that in WoD, roughly 30% or less of regular humans likely have werecreatures in their family tree if each person goes back far enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine researching your ancestry and coming to a straight-up dead end, so, out of frustration you join the Arcanum, and you then find out that your great grandmother was a literal cat, because her child (your grandparent) was a Bastet.<br /> <br /> I love how absurd Classic WoD can get. rofl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28838,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","user":"DaFrontlineSpecter","date":". 12-05-2025, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T20:18:47-08:00","id":1556217,"title":"","content":"Why would you join the Arcanum out of an interest in genealogy? Most people's don't go back that far before hitting a brick wall, or at least highly unreliable records. Unless you're from a family with a well documented history, you're going to not find it strange that you can't keep going back. And the Arcanum doesn't recruit people just to find out they're family history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T22:29:38-08:00","id":1556225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1555795#post1555795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I thought that maybe this scenario would involve the Garou being of the Japanese Hakken Tribe who are heavily influenced by human culture and have their own secret hidden packs of Japanese Wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really adds anything to the main idea, it just gives the Tribe of the child if they're a Garou (because while <i>players</i> chose their characters Tribe, <i>the characters</i> rarely do so, and anyone whose lineage is even barely known is likely to be claimed by their parents/ancestors Tribe). This is actually a problem: it gives again more things to worry about than &quot;daddy is a wolf&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">DaFrontlineSpecter</a>'s suggestions are good to make the backstory relevant to the character through the game, but the main problem is still how long the core premise itself will be relevant, and it will hardly be long, if anything at all in an actual Werewolf game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaFrontlineSpecter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1556208#post1556208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine researching your ancestry and coming to a straight-up dead end, so, out of frustration you join the Arcanum, and you then find out that your great grandmother was a literal cat, because her child (your grandparent) was a Bastet.<br /> <br /> I love how absurd Classic WoD can get. rofl.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need the Arcanum for this plot and it doesn't really help.<br /> <br /> Most people researching their ancestry in the WoD are likely to find many gaps and nothing ever comes out of it, but it may be interesting to have someone actually stumble upon some hint of the truth, enough for them to find out and, with it, the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Joining supernatural-related societies, though, is unlikely. Neither would such a character know of their existence, nor them want someone who's simply researching genealogy.<br /> <br /> After the fact, though, it all depends on how the character will react to actually finding out the supernatural at this point. It could be the backstory for a member of the Arcanum. Or, on another note, you could have someone join the Arcanum or some other faction for some other reason, and incidentally while there find out about their supernatural ancestors, but not this search being the main drive.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T01:31:43-08:00","id":1556229,"title":"","content":"Why join the Arcanum when you could just take a really, really cheap bus ride through the country and narrowly avoid dying when the inhabitants think that you're an outsider so you have to hoof it through the backroads and narrowly get clocked, only to find out that you're one of them after all?<br /> <br /> You know, the traditional way you find out about supernatural ancestry you didn't think you had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T07:12:03-08:00","id":1556237,"title":"","content":"Garou: &quot;Family dinners are so awkward when your dad is the only wolf at the table.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ananasi: &quot;I love family dinners! I ate all of my birth-siblings. My mom ate about two hundreds of my dads. I once ate half of my uncle by accident, but he's better now.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T08:58:49-08:00","id":1556238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1556237#post1556237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou: &quot;Family dinners are so awkward when your dad is the only wolf at the table.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ananasi: &quot;I love family dinners! I ate all of my birth-siblings. My mom ate about two hundreds of my dads. I once ate half of my uncle by accident, but he's better now.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, even Spiderlings only have one mom and one dad. Regardless of how many bodies they have, they're born a single spider and the rest are clones.<br /> <br /> Also remember that they still have human family members.<br /> <br /> That they also eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T09:54:53-08:00","id":1556242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555313-what-if-a-lupus-garou-bred-with-a-human-kinfolk?p=1556238#post1556238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to note, even Spiderlings only have one mom and one dad. Regardless of how many bodies they have, they're born a single spider and the rest are clones.<br /> <br /> Also remember that they still have human family members.<br /> <br /> That they also eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, but there are cases that aren't fully explained by the books: a female Ananasi can disperse herself over a large area in Crawlerling to increase her chances of encountering male spider kinfolk for mating. Female spiders can store the sperm and fertilize their eggs later; if she changes form in between or her Breed is Homid, it would be difficult to tell which one of her mates is the father. Some differences in human and spider anatomy or biology in general get really hand-wavy, even without taking into account that some of them can change sex.<br /> <br /> Overall I would say Garou are among the Fera at the easier end of the family relation spectrum. Some of the other Changing Breeds have it much more complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://foru